 with bands is the  ability to manipulate the strength curve  so the strength curve describes the way  that the difficulty changes throughout a  range of motion and this can be affected  by multiple things the angle of  resistance being one then there's  momentum when you launch yourself  through a movement then some of that  momentum is going to carry through  meaning you have to exert less force  further into the movement and then  there's the resistance the interference  provided by your own antagonist muscles  this is where compressive strength comes  in if you try and form a v-sit you'll  feel that it's hard because your own  body is getting in the way of performing  that movement the lever arm and the way  that changes so if you think about  performing a regular dumbbell curl then  as you curl the weight that's the most  difficult position because here the  lever arm is the longest the weight is  furthest from the joint so you're  effectively working against a greater  resistance then you have the elongation  of the muscle when the muscle is  completely stretched it's at its weakest  when it's completely compressed it's  also quite weak when it's right in the  middle that's where you have the most  strength usually because that's how we  use it so this is the nice thing about a  regular dumbbell curl because these two  aspects of the strength curve cancel  each other out where the weight is  heaviest your strongest and thereby this  is a fantastic tool this is harder to  accomplish with a resistance band  because the resistance band increases  its resistance as you get further as you  lengthen the band no ways to manipulate  this but that's why i'm not saying to  completely replace dumbbells and  barbells and kettlebells with bands i'm  saying to complement them with bands but  where bands then come into their own is  in allowing you to manipulate that  strength curve and plug those gaps to  strengthen yourself where your weakest  such as in those elongated positions  where you're at your end range strength  and this is really cool because it means  that now you can be powerful all the way  through that movement if you imagine  throwing a punch imagine not just  launching the punch and then losing  power as it travels but being able to  provide extra propulsion all the way  through an extra strength and that's  what you can do with the bands so you  saw me there performing a more  horizontal angled bicep curl where now  the greatest resistance is right at the  top in that compressed position where  the bicep is fully compressed because  now the resistance is coming from that  way it's trying to pull my bicep back  open this can be used to increase  mobility and by performing a weighted  stretch you can actually increase  hypertrophy because studies show that  adding resistance in a stretched  position can lead to a lot of muscle  growth and i can attest to this from  personal experience and from anecdotal  evidence so we can get into all kinds of  weighted stretch positions using the  bands which are going to help to improve  our mobility and increase hypertrophy so  don't think this doesn't apply to you if  you're a bodybuilder by the way the  ability of bands to change their  resistance like that is called linear  variable resistance  this is another big reason for farmer  strength and the kind of practical  strength that you see in dad's strength  and in physical laborers it's because  they're not just picking things off the  ground if you're thinking well i don't  have a random pole sticking out of the  ground and i don't want to go to the  field every time i train with bands how  can i train this at home then the answer  is you use something called a door  anchor you simply close the door so this  is on the other side and it can't slip  through then you can loop your band  through like that and you can do it at  the top of the door at the bottom of the  door and you can mimic pretty much  anything i've done here obviously you do  need a good amount of space in front of  the door so i admit it's not something  that everyone everyone is going to be  able to do at home but a lot of people  most people even if you're doing it in  your front door outside  so i hope you found this video useful  interesting guys if you did then please  leave a like and share it around that  helps me out immensely i'd love to hear  your comments down below let me know  what your favorite exercises using a  resistance band or resistance bands you  like training to improve not just your  strength but your strength endurance  your mobility your resilience even your  brain function then you'll probably  enjoy my ebook and training program  super functional training there's a link  to that in description down below and  there's a discount on right now during  the pandemic i also have a print book  available from all good bookshops called  functional training and beyond that's an  introduction to the concepts of  functional training and how they apply  to your everyday life as well as to  sports and athletics you can also find  these clothes in the little carousel  under this video if you like them thank  you so much for all your support and  just for watching this one please  subscribe if you want to see more like  it and hit the bell button if you want  to be notified of future uploads and  i'll see you next time thanks a ton and  bye for now

